## Why This Is Asked

Provenance and traceability are essential in real-world data pipelines; this tests ability to design end-to-end lineage with minimal components.

## Key Concepts

- Data provenance tagging
- DynamoDB as a lineage store
- Parquet with metadata for downstream queries
- DLQ handling and observability basics
- LocalStack test planning for end-to-end validation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-Lambda handler sketch to attach provenance
function handler(event){ 
  const provenance = { eventId: event.id, deviceId: event.device, firmwareVersion: event.fw, ingestionTs: Date.now(), pipelineId: 'proc-1' };
  event.provenance = provenance;
  return event;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate lineage updates in DynamoDB under retries?
- How would you extend this for cross-region replication while preserving provenance?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design robust, scalable data quality controls in a multi-tenant streaming pipeline, including schema evolution, late data handling, and quarantine workflows.

## Key Concepts

- Data quality gates and quarantines
- Per-tenant schema versions and defaults
- Idempotent writes and deduplication
- Backfill strategies and replay
- Observability with OpenTelemetry and CloudWatch

## Code Example

```javascript
// validate per-tenant event against version map
function validate(event, versionMap){
  const v = event._schemaVer ?? 1;
  const required = versionMap[v] || [];
  return required.every(f => f in event);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test quarantine and backfill reliability?
- What metrics and alarms would you configure to detect drift or failures?

## Why This Is Asked
